==Notes==
*{{LNote|Active|^|The settlement could have potentially been active as late as the ninth century of the First Era. One of the potential word walls for [[Skyrim:Slow Time|Slow Time]] mentions Aaban, a warlord from the [[Lore:Alik'r Desert|Alik'r Desert]], presumingly a [[Lore:Redguard|Redguard]].{{Ref|name=SRSlow|[[Skyrim:Slow Time#Word Wall Translations|Slow Time]] second word wall in ''[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]''}} The main [[Lore:Ra Gada|Ra Gada]] force that conquered [[Lore:Hammerfell|Hammerfell]] came to Tamriel in {{Year|1E 808}},{{Ref|name=PGE3AEM|{{Cite Book|PGE|3|All the Eras of Man}}}} but the first invasion force, led by [[Lore:Frandar Hunding|Frandar Hunding]] arrived after their exile in {{Year|1E 780}}.{{Ref|name=RHAH|{{Cite Book|Redguards, History and Heroes}}}}}}
*The [[Lore:Wing of the Crow|Wing of the Crow]] was a [[Lore:Planes of Existence|realm]] created by the [[Lore:The Crow|Crow]], a [[Lore:Luminary|Luminary of Magic]] created by Shalidor's ex-wife, [[Lore:Ulfsild the Evergreen|Archmage Ulfsild the Evergreen]]. It was shaped by its creator as a perfect trial space, and so resembled a copy of the ancient maze of Labyrinthian.{{ref|name=Crow|[[Online:The Crow|The Crow]]'s dialogue in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}}{{Ref|name=TWOTC|[[ON:The Wing of the Crow|The Wing of the Crow]] quest in [[Online:Online|ESO]]: ''[[Online:Gold Road|Gold Road]]''}}{{ref|name=ONOSP|{{Cite Book|Our Story}}}}

